<section class="hero prose">
  <h1>Not a framework.<br>A foundation.</h1>
  <p class="lede">Argot is a common vocabulary to use for any CSS project. Use a 
    standardized set of custom property names to define your own
    colors, typography, spacing, and more.</p>
  <p>By using the same variable names between projects, you reduce the cost of
    context switching and improve consistency. No dependencies needed; simply use the
    Argot template near the beginning of your stylesheet, and extend it as needed.</p>
  <div class="hero__actions">
    <a class="button-cta" href="{{ '/getting-started/' | url }}">Get started</a>
    <a href="{{ '/tokens/' | url }}">Explore the tokens →</a>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="home-section prose">
  <h2>Name the intent, not the value.</h2>
  <p>A palette step tells you what a color is. A semantic token tells you what it’s for.
    Change your palette or switch themes without rewriting every component.</p>
  <pre><code class="language-css">:root {
  /* Your primitives */
  --neutral-950: #18242b;
  --neutral-50: #f7fafb;

  /* Shared semantic names */
  --text-primary: var(--neutral-950);
  --bg-main: var(--neutral-50);
}

.card {
  color: var(--text-primary);
  background: var(--bg-main);
}</code></pre>
  <p class="note">Values shown here are illustrative. Argot supplies the vocabulary; you supply the design.</p>
</section>
<section class="home-section prose">
  <h2>One layer of your design system.</h2>
  <div class="tier-grid">
    <article><p class="eyebrow">01 / Primitive</p><h3>The raw materials</h3><p>Your palette, font families, and static values. <code>--neutral-950</code></p></article>
    <article><p class="eyebrow">02 / Semantic</p><h3>Where Argot fits</h3><p>Shared roles for those values, independent of components. <code>--text-primary</code></p></article>
    <article><p class="eyebrow">03 / Component</p><h3>The local decisions</h3><p>Optional properties scoped to individual components. <code>--card-color</code></p></article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="home-section prose">
  <h2>Ready for real projects.</h2>
  <p>The token set is deliberately defined and ready to use. Real-world adoption will help prove it out and refine it.
    Start with {{ reference.core }} core tokens, or include {{ reference.extended }} extended tokens for additional roles.</p>
  <p><a href="{{ '/getting-started/' | url }}">Try Argot in your project</a>, then
